{
 "title": "Geometry nodes 5: grass",
 "summary": "A grass blade made procedurally (Mesh Line curled with Vector Rotate by Index x Bending in Set Position, Mesh to Curve, Set Curve Radius tapered by Spline Parameter through a reversed Map Range, Curve to Mesh with a Curve Line profile), a patch of blades (Mesh Circle, Distribute Points on Faces, Instance on Points with random Z rotation and random scale), five Group Input sockets (density, patch size, rotation, height, bending) so three copies make three kinds of grass; the kinds in a collection, instanced over the landscape with Collection Info (separate and reset children). Beyond the tutorial: Pick Instance for a mix of kinds, per-patch random green shades.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "Landscape",
   "description": "the grassy hills"
  },
  {
   "name": "GrassA",
   "description": "one kind of grass patch"
  }
 ],
